cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Lean 4 sources for the near-tight lonely runner papers and the six-speed classification"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 modules (Mathlib, Lean 4.30.0) cited by three papers on sets of runner speeds with loneliness close to 1/(N+1), and the classification of six distinct positive integer speeds with loneliness at most 1/7. Overlay on the public five-speed archive; no clean-checkout build has been run; not peer reviewed. The modules were produced with substantial assistance from AI systems (Anthropic's Claude models) under the direction of the author.
authors:
